{
  "_comment": [
    "AN5b increment 2 (R281). The ONE aggregation, bound on both sides.",
    "Rows + a person's settings go in; a TeleworkInput comes out. The TypeScript side reads",
    "this file through web/lib/dossier/aggregate.ts (toTeleworkInput); the Kotlin side reads",
    "the SAME file through ch.monreleve.app.dossier.toTeleworkInput. FW12's tile defect was a",
    "second derivation of a figure the first had already produced; the way to not have it twice",
    "is to have no second unbound derivation. A one-digit change here fails BOTH builds (AC2).",
    "",
    "entries carry the full row shape (dayDate, portion, kind, absenceReason, provenance); the",
    "aggregation reads only dayDate/portion/kind - absenceReason and provenance are along for",
    "the ride so the fixture looks like a real row.",
    "",
    "expected is the TeleworkInput. granularity/denominator use the ENGINE's tags (day/halfDay,",
    "simplified240/exact), which each side maps to its own type; periodFraction is the exact",
    "double 1 - 0.05... no: remainingYearFraction output, pinned to its shortest round-trip form."
  ],
